    { q: 'A survey finds that 52% of boys and 44% of girls in Welsh secondary schools take part in organised sport three or more times a week. Interpret the data and suggest two reasons for the difference. (4 marks)', s: ['Boys’ participation is 8 percentage points higher than girls’; about half of boys, but fewer than half of girls, are highly active.', 'Reason 1: <b>body image</b> and self-consciousness, especially in adolescence, and changing-room concerns.', 'Reason 2: <b>provision and media</b> — fewer girls’ teams and clubs, less media coverage and fewer role models; stereotypes about “male” sports.', 'Strategies might include girls-only sessions, a wider range of activities and positive role models.'], a: 'Boys 8 points higher; body image, provision and stereotypes.' }
